<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n106509" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Ὑέλη</span></b> , ἡ,
			<u>Velia</u> in Lower Italy, <i><span class="en">
			Hdt.
			1.167
		</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
			Str.
			6.1.1
		</span></i>: also called <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Οὐέλιαι</span> (<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b>
				v.l.
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Βελίαι</span>
			), <i><span class="en">
				Ptol.
				<u>Geog.</u>
				3.1.8
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Οὐέλια</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					D.H.
					1.20
				</span></i>
			, who says this form is an old dialect word (<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ϝέλια</span>) for <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἑλώδη</span>
			=
			<i>marshy</i> places; but <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἕλος</span>
			prob. had no. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ϝ.</span> (The coins have
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">υελητων</span>, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">υελητεων</span>, and <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ϝελη</span>(<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">των</span>), <i>B Mus.Cat.Coins Italy</i><i><span class="en">
				pp.304,305
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				306
			</span></i>; the Oscan name <u>Velia</u> was prob. adapted as
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Υ̓ελέη</span> (hence
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Υ̓ελῆ</span> is more prob. than
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Υ̓έλη</span>) and <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Ἐλέα.</span>)</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
    <div class="alpheios-lex-alph-source">From <u>
            <u>A Greek-English Lexicon</u>
        </u> (Henry George Liddell, Robert Scott, Oxford, Clarendon Press, 1940) </div>
